WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.510
This is Monchousia, White Plume,
a leader of the Kansa, or Kaw, nation.

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.770
He came to Washington
with the delegation of 1821 and 1822.

3
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.630
Look at the formal pose,
the careful attention to clothing and jewelry,

4
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.050
and that dark, empty background.

5
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.530
King turns a specific leader into a type.

6
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:26.750
But one clue points to the real visit:
the oval silver peace medal on his chest.

7
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:30.010
President Monroe gave these medals
to the delegates.

8
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.300
Find it,

9
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.050
and you've found the diplomacy
the painting leaves out.
